---
const principles = [
  {
    title: 'Private by construction',
    body: 'Inference, embeddings and speech run on-premise. The only outbound traffic is data you asked for, like a news feed or a weather report.',
    icon: 'M12 3l7 3v5c0 4.6-3 8.4-7 10-4-1.6-7-5.4-7-10V6l7-3z',
  },
  {
    title: 'Built to run offline',
    body: 'The core loops (speech, reasoning, generation) keep working without an internet connection, because nothing in them depends on one.',
    icon: 'M4 12h16M12 4v16M6.3 6.3l11.4 11.4M17.7 6.3L6.3 17.7',
  },
  {
    title: 'Models propose, code decides',
    body: 'Fact-check verdicts, case solvability and radio instructions are checked by deterministic code before they reach a person.',
    icon: 'M5 12l4 4L19 6',
  },
];
---

<section id="lab" class="section about" aria-labelledby="lab-title">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <div class="intro">
      <p class="label" data-reveal>The lab</p>
      <h2 id="lab-title" class="h-section" data-reveal style="--delay:.06s">
        Local-first isn't a setting. It's the architecture.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="body">
      <p class="lede" data-reveal style="--delay:.1s">
        Every system we build runs its models on hardware the owner controls: one GPU workstation, or a rack in their own
        building. That constraint shapes everything. Models are chosen to fit the memory budget. Queues keep the GPU busy
        without starving interactive requests. Validation layers check model output before anyone relies on it.
      </p>
      <ul class="principles">
        {
          principles.map((p, i) => (
            <li class="principle" data-reveal style={`--delay:${0.12 + i * 0.08}s`}>
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d={p.icon} fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
              <div>
                <h3 class="h-sub">{p.title}</h3>
                <p class="muted">{p.body}</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 40px;
  }
  .intro .label {
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .principles {
    margin-top: 48px;
    display: grid;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }
  .principle {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 22px 1fr;
    gap: 20px;
    padding-block: 26px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }
  .principle svg {
    color: var(--color-ice);
    margin-top: 3px;
  }
  .principle p {
    margin-top: 8px;
    max-width: 52ch;
  }
  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 5fr 7fr;
      gap: 80px;
    }
    .intro {
      position: sticky;
      top: 120px;
      align-self: start;
    }
  }
</style>
